  <h3>Front-end and other services: OKD and GitOps</h3>
  <p>
    SPARC's front-end, IRIS, Tandem and Infofin run on an OKD (OpenShift) cluster, where merging to
    main <em>is</em> the deployment. Workloads are hardened: read-only root filesystem, non-root
    containers, SCC-constrained pods.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Merge</strong>: A merge on main is the only deployment trigger
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tekton</strong>: In-cluster pipelines build and push the images
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Argo CD</strong>: Continuously syncs the cluster to the state declared in Git
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kustomize</strong>: Per-environment overlays, no templating drift
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sealed Secrets</strong>: Secrets encrypted at rest in Git, decrypted only in the
      cluster
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
